{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Mobilisation within the first day following hip fracture surgery is recommended. However, an in-depth analysis of the association between early mobilisation and the risk of infection is lacking. OBJECTIVE: To examine the association between early mobilisation and the subsequent risk of hospital-treated infections following hip fracture surgery. METHODS: Using nationwide registries, we included 36 229 patients aged ≥65 who underwent surgery for hip fracture (2016-21). Exposure was time from surgery to first mobilisation in hours. Outcomes were any hospital-treated infection, pneumonia, urinary tract infection and sepsis within 2-30 days and reoperation due to surgical-site infection within 2-365 days of surgery. We calculated cumulative incidences (risks), risk differences (RD) and hazard ratios (HR) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) using the inverse probability of treatment (IPT) weighted method to account for confounding. RESULTS: Overall, 27 174 (75%) patients were mobilised ≤24 h, 2890 (8%) between 24 and 36 h, and 6165 (17%) were mobilised >36 h of surgery or had no registration of mobilisation time.In the weighted analysis, the risk of any infection was 12.9% (CI 11.7%-14.2%) in patients mobilised 24-36 h of surgery and 10.9% (CI 10.5%-11.7%) in those mobilised ≤24 h, corresponding to RD of 2.0% (CI 0.7-3.3) and HR of 1.2 (CI 1.1-1.3). Similar associations were observed for pneumonia and urinary tract infection but not for sepsis and reoperation. CONCLUSIONS: Infection is a common complication after hip fracture surgery. Mobilisation within 24 h is clearly associated with reduced infection risk. Our results emphasise the importance of early mobilisation and suggest a possible pathway for reducing complications and mortality after hip fracture.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Thomas Johannesson","Andersen, Ina Trolle","Kristensen, Morten Tange","Pedersen, Alma Becic"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-793484"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hjelholt, Thomas Johannesson"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cumulated ambulation score","Denmark epidemiology","Early Ambulation statistics numerical data","Female","Hip Fractures surgery","Hip fracture","Humans","Incidence","Infection","Male","Mobilisation","Older people","Pneumonia epidemiology","Registries","Reoperation statistics numerical data","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Surgical Wound Infection prevention control","Time Factors","Urinary Tract Infections epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early mobilisation after hip fracture surgery reduces the risk of infection an inverse probability of treatment weighted analysis","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85216089678","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.94-793484","identifier":[{"id":"85216089678","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39838916","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f3dd5cc6-58de-4b24-8568-748e5b44ea22","ku-e8b2ca13-22e2-4644-aeb0-cee2c56a13f0"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Denmark/epidemiology","Early Ambulation/statistics & numerical data","Female","Hip Fractures/surgery","Humans","Incidence","Male","Pneumonia/epidemiology","Registries","Reoperation/statistics & numerical data","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Surgical Wound Infection/prevention & control","Time Factors","Urinary Tract Infections/epidemiology","cumulated ambulation score","hip fracture","infection","mobilisation","older people"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC51A90AF19A45F4D73FD1B20306EA66"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Ældresygdomme"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Johannesson","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"e22aa9dd-c881-4afe-a9cb-55a9f34bc851","name":"Hjelholt, Thomas Johannesson","orcid":"0000-0003-0112-5801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ina Trolle","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"44e5a828-24b1-4b05-9134-7dfb490435a1","name":"Andersen, Ina Trolle","orcid":"0000-0002-8140-1548","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Morten Tange","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"4fd22e3d-c23b-4041-843e-a410b424cb05","name":"Kristensen, Morten Tange","orcid":"0000-0001-5868-4677","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alma Becic","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"797cacd6-5e68-4aac-a0fa-db74425f732b","name":"Pedersen, Alma Becic","orcid":"0000-0002-3288-9401","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39838916"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ageing/afaf007","issn":["00020729","14682834"],"issn_org":["00020729"],"issue":"1","journal":"Age and Ageing","paperid":"afaf007","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Age and Ageing","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216089678"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f3dd5cc6-58de-4b24-8568-748e5b44ea22","ku-e8b2ca13-22e2-4644-aeb0-cee2c56a13f0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Early mobilisation after hip fracture surgery reduces the risk of infection : an inverse probability of treatment weighted analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-793484","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Key summary points: To examine the association between early mobilization after hip fracture surgery and the risk of long-term opioid therapy at 1-year follow-up. Findings: Long-term opioid therapy is a common complication after hip fracture surgery. Mobilization within 24 h after surgery is associated with a lower risk of long-term opioid therapy compared to mobilization between 24 and 36 h. Message: Early mobilization is one of the key elements of the successful patient recovery for reducing risk of complications and mortality after hip fracture surgery. Purpose: Abstract: Early mobilization after hip fracture operation is associated with better clinical outcomes, but its impact on long-term opioid therapy (LTOT) remains unclear. Methods: Using Danish population-based registries we included patients aged ≥ 65 who underwent surgery for a first-time hip fracture between 2016 and 2021 (n = 36,229). LTOT was defined as redeeming ≥ 2 prescriptions between 31 and 365 days of surgery. Using stabilized inverse probability of treatment (sIPT) weighing, we calculated risks and risk differences with 95% confidence intervals (CI) for opioid use balancing mobilization groups ≤ 24 h vs 24–36 h on measured confounders and taking death into consideration. Results: 67.3% of all patients were women and the median age was 82.6 years (75.8; 88.6). 75% of patients were mobilized ≤ 24 h of surgery, whereas 8% were mobilized between 24 and 36 h, 4.9% > 36 h, and 12.1% had missing data on mobilization. Patients mobilized ≤ 24 h and 24–36 h were similar in age, fracture type, and marital status, but those mobilized ≤ 24 h had fewer comorbidities, better pre-fracture mobility, and a higher social position. They also had a lower risk of LTOT (29.99%) compared to those mobilized 24–36 h (33.42%), with a weighted risk difference of 3.44% (95% CI 1.58–5.30). Conclusions: LTOT is common after hip fracture surgery. Mobilization ≤ 24 h after surgery is associated with a lower risk of LTOT compared to mobilization between 24 and 36 h. Early mobilization is one of the key elements of successful patient recovery for reducing complications and mortality after hip fracture surgery.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tudorache, Yasmina Maria","Andersen, Ina Trolle","Hjelholt, Thomas Johannesson","Kristensen, Morten Tange","Sheehan, Katie J","Pedersen, Alma Becic"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-813651"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London"],"keyword":["Early mobilization","Epidemiology","Geriatrics","Hip fracture","Opioid use","Rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between early mobilization after hip fracture surgery and risk of long term opioid therapy","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-025-01227-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-813651","identifier":[{"id":"40332660","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12174293","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105004467553","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-606b6015-b6c8-4d81-a389-01c9f78a0e72","ku-a6ac69a0-475a-479f-a5a3-2603995b7c89"],"keyword":["Early mobilization","Epidemiology","Geriatrics","Hip fracture","Opioid use","Rehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7D95FE802B1CE0BFF3A9F53FCF0CD9F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/454293973/s41999-025-01227-7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-025-01227-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yasmina Maria","key":"tudorachepau","last":"Tudorache","locid":"61c3f90e-08f8-4ef3-a5a7-15a9778e53ca","name":"Tudorache, Yasmina Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ina Trolle","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"44e5a828-24b1-4b05-9134-7dfb490435a1","name":"Andersen, Ina Trolle","orcid":"0000-0002-8140-1548","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas J","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"e22aa9dd-c881-4afe-a9cb-55a9f34bc851","name":"Hjelholt, Thomas Johannesson","name_org":"Hjelholt, Thomas J","orcid":"0000-0003-0112-5801","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Morten Tange","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"4fd22e3d-c23b-4041-843e-a410b424cb05","name":"Kristensen, Morten Tange","orcid":"0000-0001-5868-4677","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Katie J","key":"sheehanpau","last":"Sheehan","name":"Sheehan, Katie J","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alma B","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"797cacd6-5e68-4aac-a0fa-db74425f732b","name":"Pedersen, Alma Becic","name_org":"Pedersen, Alma B","orcid":"0000-0002-3288-9401","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40332660"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s41999-025-01227-7","issn":["18787649"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Geriatric Medicine","pages":"921-931","paperid":"e1863","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"European Geriatric Medicine","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004467553"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-606b6015-b6c8-4d81-a389-01c9f78a0e72","ku-a6ac69a0-475a-479f-a5a3-2603995b7c89"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association between early mobilization after hip fracture surgery and risk of long-term opioid therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-813651","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores the intricate dynamics of digital welfare within the context of late-capitalist welfare states, focusing on the advanced digitalisation initiatives of Denmark. It offers a critical analysis of the concept of ‘digital welfare’ – defined as the integration of digital technologies into the frameworks of social protection. Central to the research is how the Danish welfare state, recognised for its e-government leadership, engages with and incorporates critiques to sustain its approach to digital transformation. Utilising Boltanski’s theories on the absorption of capitalist critique and Mathiesen’s ‘silently silencing’ concept, the study examines the state’s proficiency in assimilating criticism. The findings reveal the persistent flexibility of late-capitalist governance systems, especially in how digital welfare policies are leveraged to reconnect citizens with state mechanisms while simultaneously mitigating dissent. The research highlights the necessity for ongoing investigation into the implications of digitalisation for welfare institutions and societal structures at large.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754083"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital welfare","Nordic welfare states","Public sector digitalisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the absorbent digital welfare state silencing dissent steering progress","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-754083","identifier":[{"id":"85193945743","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a25e3bb7-b7b8-4c2c-a55f-ed7d62f20c22"],"keyword":["Digital welfare","Nordic welfare states","critique absorption","late-capitalist governance","public sector digitalisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-57B50ACF87D45F67C78F29A21A27BD8F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-a25e3bb7-b7b8-4c2c-a55f-ed7d62f20c22"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Absorbent Digital Welfare State : Silencing dissent steering progress","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754083","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Digitaliseringen har gennem de seneste årtier transformeret næsten alle aspekter af vores samfund, fra den måde vi kommunikerer på, til den måde vi forvalter vores demokratiske institutioner. Denne forandring har ikke kun medført teknologiske forandringer, men også rejst nye spørgsmål om magt og styring i mødet mellem borgeren og staten (Schou & Hjelholt 2019, Scupola 2018). Centralt for denne forandring står at digitalisering ikke blot er anvendelse af neutrale redskaber, men derimod noget der direkte omformer sociale strukturer og magtrelationer. Digitaliseringen bliver ofte præsenteret som positivt, naturligt og uundgåeligt. Den kommer f.eks. med håb om hurtigere sagsbehandling, mere transparens for borgeren og en gennemgående idé om, at der kan spares penge ved omlægning til digitale forløb (Milakovich 2014, Schou & Hjelholt 2018). Ved nærmere eftersyn bidrager den stigende digitalisering dog også til at konsolidere eksisterende magtstrukturer og besværliggøre dialog med store grupper af samfundet (Helsper & Reisdorf 2017, Hjelholt & Papazu 2021). I et magtperspektiv, der vil undersøge hvordan relationen mellem staten og borgeren forandrer sig, bliver det centralt at komme nærmere hvordan digitalisering udspiller sig i praksis. Ikke blot hos borgeren og sagsbehandleren, men også hvad det er for en digitaliseringsramme hvori de navigerer. Derfor er studiet af, hvorledes staten responderer på kritik også en del af en interesse i hvordan den digitale dagsorden formes, legitimeres og fremmes samt hvilke interesser disse tjener.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747219"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital transformation","Power relations","Social structures","State citizen interaction","Technological governance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digitaliseringsmagt kritik og fremskridt","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-747219","ids":["itu-3bc193a6-c5c5-4ef0-9964-0f1f2107f883"],"keyword":["Digital transformation","Power relations","Social structures","State-citizen interaction","Technological governance"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-51D78908029905C8956A0F8E63BEA8E0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3bc193a6-c5c5-4ef0-9964-0f1f2107f883"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digitaliseringsmagt: Kritik og Fremskridt","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747219","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Denmark is often highlighted as a pioneer in public digitalization. Since 2015, digital self-service has been mandatory for Danish citizens for most public services and benefits. This represents a significant shift in citizens’ interaction with public authorities and places numerous demands on both citizens and authorities. We ask: How does public digitalization, including mandatory digital self-service and automation, affect citizens’ administrative burdens when they apply for public services in Denmark? We present a qualitative empirical study based on interviews, surveys, and observations with citizens and practitioners from the authorities Labour Market Supplementary Pension (ATP) and Udbetaling Danmark (Disbursement Denmark) (UDK). We investigate how the policy design and implementation of digital services affect citizens’ administrative burdens when they apply for pension and parental leave. The decision to introduce mandatory digital self-service initially resulted in increased administrative burdens for many citizens. However, ATP and UDK have subsequently reduced citizens’ administrative burdens through automation and by using data-driven analytics and qualitative research to improve their self-service solutions and communication. In line with previous studies, we see that the effects of digitalization are distributed both within and across service areas. There is a particular difference in the extent and type of administrative burdens that citizens in Denmark and abroad experience when they apply for public benefits. Finally, we see that both benefit and state characteristics influence public authorities’ possibility to reduce administrative burdens.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Østergaard Madsen, Christian","Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776389"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ATP","Administrative burden","Administrative byrder","Digitalisering","Digitalization","Udbetaling Danmark","public benefits","self service"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digitalisering og administrative byrder","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/politica.v56i4.151661","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776389","ids":["itu-3ad0780a-90fa-42d4-b26f-db3a69de3a91"],"keyword":["ATP","Administrative burden","Digitalization","Udbetaling Danmark","administrative byrder","digitalisering","offentlige ydelser","public benefits","self-service","selvbetjening"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5C9FBC2F26197C19EC5BA57CE7AAFCD1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/politica.v56i4.151661","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Danish Institute for IT Program Management","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"østergaardmadsenpau","last":"Østergaard Madsen","locid":"74a08deb-18e1-48d0-a86e-ed6675da92ab","name":"Østergaard Madsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5984-561X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/politica.v56i4.151661","issn":["01050710","2246042X"],"issn_org":["01050710"],"issue":"4","journal":"Politica - Tidsskrift for politisk videnskab","pages":"296","paperid":"1","publisher":"Syddansk Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"Politica - Tidsskrift for politisk videnskab","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3ad0780a-90fa-42d4-b26f-db3a69de3a91"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digitalisering og administrative byrder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776389","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Thomas Johannesson","Andersen, Ina Trolle","Tange Kristensen, Morten","Pedersen, Alma Becic"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-787578"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early mobilization following hip fracture surgery and subsequent risk of infection","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-024-01090-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-787578","ids":["au-9112509e-5073-4758-8bb2-a630c13a95cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-6-6-3849A2D2E6061826B5C2ABA08B167CD9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-024-01090-y","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Ældresygdomme"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Johannesson","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"e22aa9dd-c881-4afe-a9cb-55a9f34bc851","name":"Hjelholt, Thomas Johannesson","orcid":"0000-0003-0112-5801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ina Trolle","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"44e5a828-24b1-4b05-9134-7dfb490435a1","name":"Andersen, Ina Trolle","orcid":"0000-0002-8140-1548","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","cor