{"abstract":"The Danish welfare state is one of the most digitally advanced in the world, and with digitalization reaching the forefront of the political agenda, the citizen has been expected to perform a transformation similar to that of the state toward ‘becoming digital’ (see Pors 2005). Since 2014, when it became mandatory for all Danish citizens to communicate with the state through the digital infrastructure ‘Digital Post’, digital citizenship as such has become a mandatory part of being a Danish citizen. With this ideal of the Digital Citizen, new exclusionary mechanisms have emerged, as not all citizens manage to live up to the requirements of The Digital State. In this paper, we use interviews and case stories to analyse the position of these partially or non-digital citizens vis-à-vis a state which is becoming increasingly concerned with including them, not least through the (re-)establishment of an ‘inclusion office’ in the national Digitalisation Agency. If this inclusion does not succeed, it is feared, the non-digital citizens will become invisible to the state, and the state in its new, digital reconfiguration will be out of reach for them. At the same time, for the digital citizen, the state has more entry points than ever before, giving rise to new forms of societal inequality. The renewed concern that the state shows these ‘problematic’ citizens, e.g., through its ‘inclusion office’, can be conceptualized as a type of ‘care’ with new, built-in power dynamics (Bellacasa 2010) that we wish to unpack.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina","Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382272"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Danish welfare state","Digital Citizenship","Digital Exclusion","Digital Inequality","Inclusion Office"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the inclusion office","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382272","ids":["itu-43bd23e8-9c66-4126-ac2d-8e03273c291d"],"keyword":["Danish Welfare State","Digital Citizenship","Digital Exclusion","Digital Inequality","Inclusion Office"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9CE9D487D6D06C231AFE03B9942C0F40"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6ec63914-1f4e-4708-8830-1b054c2ee03a","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-43bd23e8-9c66-4126-ac2d-8e03273c291d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Inclusion Office","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382272","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383718"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital marginalisering af udsatte ældre arbejdsrapport","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383718","ids":["itu-a86968c7-85c0-463a-8ebe-ba3c550f9556"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3675A6515EE709CAD989AD86C7298D1A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a86968c7-85c0-463a-8ebe-ba3c550f9556"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital marginalisering af udsatte ældre : Arbejdsrapport","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383718","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In the last several decades welfare states have increasingly used digital technologies as a means of both delivering welfare services to citizens (Eriksson 2012) and restructuring public sector institutions (Henman, 2010; Henman & Dean 2010). Dating back to the early 1950s (Margetts, 2009) government officials have often thought digital technologies as offering simple, technical solutions to complex organizational problems. Such officials have touted digitalization as an almost magical means of making public institutions more flexible, innovative and efficient. Existing research on ‘e-government’ and ‘digital era governance’, however, has tended to neglect questions of statehood, politics and spatiality. This neglect of spatiality stands in stark contrast to the work of radical geographers and critical sociologists. Such scholars have consistently emphasized that state spatiality is a continuously unfolding, variegated and conflictual set of processes (Brenner, 2004a; Lefebvre, 2009; Peck, 2001); in addition, researchers in this area are producing a growing body of work concerned precisely with the new digital geographies now being constructed (Ash, Kitchin, et al., 2018). Exploring phenomena such as ‘Smart Cities’ (Tironi & Valderrama, 2018; Vanolo, 2014) and surveillance technologies for mapping urban crime (Jefferson, 2017; Wiig, 2018), this research has demonstrated how new spaces of discipline, inclusion and exclusion as well as state power are coming into being. The aim in this paper is to contribute to the ongoing conversation regarding the spatiality of capitalist states in general and the emergence of digital spaces in particular. I wish to do so by focusing on some of the more mundane forms of state spatiality that are currently being constructed through processes of public sector digitalization. During recent decades citizen service centers have been transformed as most people are supposed to act as digital citizens and this paper reports on a two-year empirical study of new spaces and frontiers of welfare professionals. In advancing the concept of new digital state spatiality, I hope to demonstrate how digital infrastructures, political discourses, public sector institutions and citizens are collectively forming new and layered spatial configurations. In addition to providing important insights into contemporary processes of state restructuring and rescaling, the articulation of this new concept paves the way for further conceptual and empirical work on the state spaces forged under contemporary conditions of entrenched neoliberalism and advanced digitalization.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382071"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital welfare","Inclusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish welfare state and digital spatiality spaces of inclusion and exclusion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382071","ids":["itu-369fa652-a244-4cde-bdda-c613ca4a3b95"],"keyword":["Digital welfare","Inclusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8FA55046BC900D892C052FA3D7333A4A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-369fa652-a244-4cde-bdda-c613ca4a3b95"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The danish welfare state and digital spatiality : Spaces of inclusion and exclusion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382071","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Hjelholt og Papazu peger på behovet for at bevæge sig ud over et fokus på den enkeltes kompetencer, når digitaliseringens slagsider diskuteres. De belyser, hvordan offentlig digitalisering fører til en rumlig reorganisering af velfærdsstaten, med forandrede offentlige-digitale rum der skaber nye oplevelser af mødet med staten. De analyserer digitalt udsatte borgeres oplevelse af den digitale offentlige sektor. De beskriver hvordan det digitale velfærdssamfund favner og kommer tættere på den digitalt selvhjulpne borger, men trækker sig tilbage fra den borger der ikke formår at betjene sig selv og blive oplært i hjælp til selvhjælp.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Papazu, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382330"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digitally excluded citizens","Information society","Public digitalisation","Spatial reorganisation","Welfare state"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"de har fået nemid men det er ikke nemt for mig digital rum me lighed i den danske velfærdsstat","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86131451/FINAL_De_har_f_et_NemID.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382330","ids":["itu-475446c2-c117-48d6-8a25-e66d40a63c49"],"keyword":["Digitally excluded citizens","Information society","Public digitalisation","Spatial reorganisation","Welfare state"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-26935A27F6040CC00150A1571CC764EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86131451/FINAL_De_har_f_et_NemID.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6ec63914-1f4e-4708-8830-1b054c2ee03a","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09043535"],"issue":"163","journal":"Social Kritik:Tidsskrift for social analyse & debat","publisher":"Selskabet til Fremme af Social Debat","status":"p","title":"Social Kritik:Tidsskrift for social analyse & debat","volume":"2021-2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-475446c2-c117-48d6-8a25-e66d40a63c49"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"\"De har fået NemID, men det er ikke nemt for mig” - Digital rum(me)lighed i den danske velfærdsstat","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382330","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Growth hormone (GH) exerts IGF-I dependent protein anabolic and direct lipolytic effects. Obesity reversibly suppresses GH secretion driven by elevated FFA levels, whereas serum IGF-I levels remain normal or elevated due to elevated portal insulin levels. Fasting in lean individuals suppresses hepatic IGF-I production and increases pituitary GH release, but this pattern is less pronounced in obesity. Fasting in obesity is associated with increased sensitivity to the insulin-antagonistic effects of GH. GH treatment in obesity induces a moderate reduction in fat mass and an increase in lean body mass but the therapeutic potential is uncertain.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Astrid Johannesson","Høgild, Morten Lyng","Bak, Ann Mosegaard","Arlien-Søborg, Mai Christiansen","Bæk, Amanda","Jessen, Niels","Richelsen, Bjørn","Pedersen, Steen Bønløkke","Møller, Niels","Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263586"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde"],"keyword":["Growth hormone","Insulin Like Growth Factor I","Obesity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"growth hormone and obesity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85083344829","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263586","identifier":[{"id":"85083344829","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32418587","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-eb3746bd-be4a-42c0-9bca-638f7635c0a9"],"keyword":["Growth hormone","Insulin-like growth factor I","Obesity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9BDF27DE27A5433140DAE2380169422"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medical Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Astrid","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"7c969e96-fa50-4878-a9fe-bea51d76ec75","name":"Hjelholt, Astrid Johannesson","name_org":"Hjelholt, Astrid","orcid":"0000-0002-3114-4176","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"høgildpau","last":"Høgild","locid":"d188742e-e315-4edc-9d28-9172dd82bb18","name":"Høgild, Morten Lyng","name_org":"Høgild, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann Mosegaard","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"ffbd7f60-6843-425d-b7ea-8c4527ee469b","name":"Bak, Ann Mosegaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mai Christiansen","key":"arliensøborgpau","last":"Arlien-Søborg","locid":"008fd532-bc75-466c-883a-45acf52cb7c1","name":"Arlien-Søborg, Mai Christiansen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amanda","key":"bækpau","last":"Bæk","locid":"32f3a9e7-a5c5-403c-b6e4-579c89d36ce9","name":"Bæk, Amanda","orcid":"0009-0005-1500-5466","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"f0d20e5e-d5b5-44da-980e-3e052af18b46","name":"Jessen, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5613-7274","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjørn","key":"richelsenpau","last":"Richelsen","locid":"533f94a0-9c20-41c4-a24a-3fb662601c40","name":"Richelsen, Bjørn","orcid":"0009-0007-9383-546X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Bønløkke","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"6fbce58b-23e6-41fa-b756-0b9558645564","name":"Pedersen, Steen Bønløkke","orcid":"0000-0002-7838-8063","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"2e0d8e2a-2da1-4d55-b2da-0a25c0375b1e","name":"Møller, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5627-7322","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Otto","key":"lundejørgensenpau","last":"Lunde Jørgensen","locid":"303ebe86-6861-4b19-b4d7-6bda0526b27e","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","name_org":"Lunde Jørgensen, Jens Otto","orcid":"0000-0001-7408-1526","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32418587"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ecl.2020.02.009","issn":["08898529","15584410"],"issn_org":["08898529"],"issue":"2","journal":"Endocrinology & Metabolism Clinics of North America","pages":"239-250","publisher":"WB  Saunders","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders","status":"p","title":"Endocrinology & Metabolism Clinics of North America","title_org":"Endocrinology and Metabolism Clinics of North America","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083344829"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eb3746bd-be4a-42c0-9bca-638f7635c0a9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Growth Hormone and Obesity","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263586","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Welfare professionals’ work practices are changing significantly, as public sectors across the world are undergoing extensive digital transformations. States roll out grand digitalization and automation projects with a promise of higher efficiency and better quality in the public sector. However, the extensive digital transformation also put welfare professionals’ sense of professionalism at stake. Based on 13 interviews with welfare professionals, we in this paper explore how they experience a sense of alienation in relation to the digitalization of their work. We identify two experiences of alienation: (1) meaninglessness: a lack of human connection and (2) powerlessness: a sense of forced ignorance. These experiences of alienation challenge the welfare professionals’ job satisfaction as well as how they assess the cases of the citizens.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørring, Louise","Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-088.46-031397"],"event":{"end":"2020-07-04","place":"Hamburg, de","start":"2020-07-02","title":"36th EGOS Colloquium 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Alienation","Digital Inequality","Digital transformation","Digitalization","Public Sector Efficiency","Public sector","Sense of Professionalism","Welfare professionals"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"meaninglessness and powerlessness alienation among welfare professionals in the digital public sector","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://www.egosnet.org/2020/hamburg/Colloquium_PROGRAM","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.46-031397","ids":["cbs-3ea0478e-cb9d-450d-881c-09daa8d1c62d","itu-365c006a-e94a-4805-833d-9a496fdad962"],"keyword":["Alienation","Digital Transformation","Digital inequality","Digitalization","Public Sector Efficiency","Public sector","Sense of Professionalism","Welfare professionals"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-3AAD573DCA6A3C683D8A4B79F00C409E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/62099103/louise_joerring_et_al_meaninglessness_and_powerlessness_conference_paper_egos_2020.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://www.egosnet.org/2020/hamburg/Colloquium_PROGRAM","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"jørringpau","last":"Jørring","locid":"2127799b-efdf-439c-84d0-545191571a47","name":"Jørring, Louise","orcid":"0009-0006-7425-6828","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-3ea0478e-cb9d-450d-881c-09daa8d1c62d","itu-365c006a-e94a-4805-833d-9a496fdad962"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Meaninglessness and Powerlessness : Alienation Among Welfare Professionals in the Digital Public Sector","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.46-031397","year":"2020","yearsub":2021}
{"abstract":"Den danske offentlige sektor har gennemgået en række storstilede digitaliseringsreformer over de sidste årtier. Disse har på afgørende vis været med til at forandre sektoren indefra såvel som udadtil: fra at være et primært internt anliggende mellem ministerier, styrelser, forvaltninger og kom¬muner er digitale platforme i stigende grad blevet en grundlæggende præmis for mødet med borgere. I denne artikel beskriver vi, hvordan digitaliseringsreformer har udviklet sig siden starten af 1990'erne, og viser, hvordan disse strategier har været med til at præge interaktionen med borgere i velfærdsstatens frontlinje. På baggrund af disse beskrivelser reflekterer vi over nogle af de indbyggede dilemmaer, der skabes i bestræbelserne på at digitalisere den offentlige sektor. Vi diskuterer i øvrigt, hvordan digitalisering forholder sig til eksisterende styringsparadigmer. Samlet set leverer artiklen dermed et bidrag til den eksisterende forvaltnings- og velfærdstatsforskning. Vi viser, hvordan det omfattende og komplekse arbejde med digitalisering har sat dybe spor i den danske velfærdsstat.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Schou, Jannick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383584"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Borgerservice","Digitalisering","Forvaltningsreformer","Offentlig sektor","Velfærdsstat"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digitalisering af den danske offentlige sektor hvor er vi på vej hen","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85790852/2_2019_4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383584","ids":["itu-9f1e769b-5a0e-4710-a885-443514977054"],"keyword":["Borgerservice","Digitalisering","Forvaltningsreformer","Offentlig sektor","Velfærdsstat"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DE9AD8061EC424B5361BD33B82F746F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85790852/2_2019_4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannick","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Jannick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01050710","2246042X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Politica - Tidsskrift for politisk videnskab","status":"p","title":"Politica - Tidsskrift for politisk videnskab","title_org":"Økonomi og Politik","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9f1e769b-5a0e-4710-a885-443514977054"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digitalisering af den danske offentlige sektor: hvor er vi på vej hen?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383584","year":"2019","yearsub":"2021"}
