{"abstract":"The shadow of Big Data: data-citizenship and exclusion Big data are understood as being able to provide insights on human behaviour at an individual as well as at an aggregated societal level (Manyka et al. 2011). These insights are expected to be more detailed and precise than anything before thanks to the large volume of digital data and to the unobstrusive nature of the data collection (Fishleigh 2014). Within this perspective, these two dimensions (volume and unobstrusiveness) define contemporary big data techniques as a socio-technical offering to society, a live representation of itself. More precisely, within a system theory approach (Luhmann 1982, 2010), large-scale big data work as a boundary-drawing operation where the difference between the system and its environment is reproduced. Here the result of system observation is defined by what is made visible as (big) data. Within this process \"data-citizenship\" emerges. Data-citizenship assumes that citizens will be visible to the state through the data they produce. On a general level data-citizenship shifts citizenship from an intrinsic status of a group of people to a status achieved through action. This approach assumes equal possibilities of action for every citizen, even if research has shown that an unequal distribution of participatory potential is unavoidable (boyd & Crawford 2012). Data-citizenships echoes what was envisioned by Luhmann (2010): When society is defined through the metacode of inclusion/exclusion, persons (of which citizens are equivalent within the legal system) are emancipated depending on their ability of being data producers. We will present preliminary results of an ongoing research about the digitalisation process in the Danish public sector. Through the analysis of specific examples we will show how those citizens who do not leave (digital) traces not only appear at the margins or entirely disappear (Bourdieu 1999) in the shadow of big-data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rossi, Luca","Hjelholt, Morten","Neumayer, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383362"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["social systems big data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the shadow of big data data citizenship and exclusion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383362","ids":["itu-8e6deaf9-0fec-4f5b-aad2-8731d82d796a"],"keyword":["social systems, big data,"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D47C643E26F33E7111CA995DC0E5F8B9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games","The Department, Digital Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","locid":"1b45e3f5-b8cd-4c0d-a444-2901304f76ee","name":"Rossi, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-3629-2039","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"neumayerpau","last":"Neumayer","name":"Neumayer, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8e6deaf9-0fec-4f5b-aad2-8731d82d796a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Shadow of Big Data: Data-Citizenship and Exclusion","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383362","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Formålet med det projekt, som Kulturstyrelsen og Medierådet for Børn og Unge har iværksat, er at fore-tage et afdækningsstudie, der skal ”identificere og prioritere centrale elementer, der er særligt relevante at medtage i en [eventuel fremtidig] undersøgelse af media literacy-niveauet i den danske befolkning. [Herunder] identifikation af behov og udfordringer samt prioritering af media literacy-elementer, der er særligt relevante for videre fokus og monitorering i Danmark”. Det har samtidig været afgørende og et krav i forbindelse med gennemførelsen af undersøgelsen at inddrage de personer ”det handler om”. Det vil sige, at undersøgelsen ikke blot består af viden fra forskere og myndigheder, men har haft fokus på at inddrage den danske befolkning. Desuden har studiet haft et bredt sigte, således at fokus ikke afgrænser sig til en bestemt gruppe, som eksempelvis børn eller ældre, men inkluderer et bredt udsnit af befolknin-gen på tværs af alder, bopæl, baggrund og mediebrug. Det udførte afdækningsstudie er baseret på eksisterende litteratur og analyser samt en omfattende kva-litativ undersøgelse. Den kvalitative undersøgelse er udarbejdet særskilt til dette afdækningsstudie og indgår med særlig vægt i analysen. I den kvalitative undersøgelse har vi set nærmere på relationer mel-lem danskeres mediebrug i hverdagslivet, mediekompetencer samt refleksioner over mediernes betyd-ning, samt muligheder og udfordringer i deltagernes egen tilværelse. I undersøgelsen deltog 20 forskelli-ge familier, fordelt på landets fem regioner. Undersøgelsen var bygget op omkring et metodisk apparat, som bygger på fire forskellige fokusområder: Kontekst, adgang, brug samt kritisk forståelse. Rapportens sidste del præsenterer anbefalinger til udformning af en fremtidig, omfattende, modul-baseret undersøgelse af danskernes mediekompetencer og media literacy niveau, herunder en gennem-gang af relevante elementer i forhold til de overordnede fokusområder, som foreslås. Der peges endelig på en række udfordringer, der er identificeret såvel i forhold til den foreslåede undersøgelses design og indhold, som i forhold til gennemførelsen af de enkelte moduler.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stald, Gitte Bang","Hjelholt, Morten","Nielsen, Laura Høvsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382309"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Media literacy kompetencer medier Danmark"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"media literacy i en dansk kontekst specialrapport","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382309","ids":["itu-460e35ac-82ce-4beb-8bfe-f66173b62735"],"keyword":["Media literacy; kompetencer; medier; Danmark"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4DF181107F2B9B4CCFC66B5840E7CA88"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte Bang","key":"staldpau","last":"Stald","locid":"b752c464-c7fb-4a52-a0c3-3b2d3db5d62f","name":"Stald, Gitte Bang","orcid":"0000-0002-2588-6261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Høvsgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Laura Høvsgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"105","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-460e35ac-82ce-4beb-8bfe-f66173b62735"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Media literacy i en dansk kontekst : SPECIALRAPPORT","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382309","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754066"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discussion on the basis of scientific calculation of labor remuneration in the contract system of enterprise economy","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://sjis.scandinavian-iris.org/index.php/sjis/article/view/87","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754066","ids":["itu-216b8c68-ee99-4a9b-9654-bf7625c2ee88"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69CF7475727FFE5678C05D23113F8FD1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09050167"],"issn_org":["19010990"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","publisher":"Association for Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-216b8c68-ee99-4a9b-9654-bf7625c2ee88"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discussion on the basis of scientific calculation of labor remuneration in the contract system of enterprise economy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754066","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This work-in-progress paper reports on preliminary findings from 15 interviews with so called “non-digital” Danish citizens to address and problematize this classification as a social category. In linking classification theory (the categories used in the digital post system) to a notion of advanced digital marginalization (to portray the path dependency of those who struggle to maintain links to societal membership) the paper expose the complexity of the “non-digital” and discusses how the assembling and connection of certain people, as a starting point for governmental strategies, might distort and prevent insights into how individuals and social groups are (re)-produced into new socio-technical configurations. The paper presents preliminary findings that suggest that “non-digitals” are in fact digital users but not in a way that allows them to be categorised as such. Finally the paper outline how further work will use the concept of advanced digital marginalization, to elaborate on these findings.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384921"],"event":{"end":"2015-03-16","place":"Madeira, pt","start":"2015-03-14","title":"13th International Conference on e-Society 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Classification theory","Digital marginalization","Digital post system","Non digital citizens","Socio technical configurations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the digital outcasts advanced margins in digital societies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384921","ids":["itu-f8343bfb-a172-4fc0-a5cd-708d4a0e7c41"],"keyword":["Classification theory","Digital marginalization","Digital post system","Non-digital citizens","Socio-technical configurations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-173731FAEA0509E569958335B0247E47"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Piet","key":"kommerspedh","last":"Kommers","name":"Kommers, Piet","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pedro","key":"isaiaspedh","last":"Isaias","name":"Isaias, Pedro","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789898533326"],"pages":"239-243","publisher":"International Association for Development, IADIS","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th International Conference e-Society 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f8343bfb-a172-4fc0-a5cd-708d4a0e7c41"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Digital Outcasts - Advanced Margins in Digital Societies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384921","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"IT projects are often complex arrangements of technological components, social actions, and organizational transformation that are difficult to manage in practice. This paper takes an analytical discourse perspective to explore the process of legitimizing IT projects. We introduce the concept of resonating statements to highlight how central actors navigate in various discourses over time. Particularly, the statements and actions of an IT project manager are portrayed to show how individuals can legitimize actions by connecting statements to historically produced discourses. The case study of an IT project in a Danish local government spans a two-year time period and demonstrates a double- loop legitimization process. First, resonating statements are produced to localize a national IT initiative to support the specificity of a local government discourse. Second, the resonating statements are used as part of a feedback loop to re-attach the localized IT project to the broader national discourse. The paper concludes with reflections on how to actively build on resonating statements as a strategic resource for legitimizing IT projects.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Jensen, Tina Blegind"],"cuid":["S02-099.84-031604"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Case study","Discourse","IT projects","resonating statement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resonating statements discursive acts in it projects","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1413&context=sjis","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.84-031604","identifier":[{"id":"84952773872","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-655003c9-6f4b-4adb-a2d8-467011b8c2f2","itu-547f4d5a-db69-4dd7-b3e6-709bca4adcf4"],"keyword":["IT projects","case study","discourse","resonating statement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3AEDFFB1267F080B342EA14CE66669CC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1413&context=sjis","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://iris.cs.aau.dk/tl_files/volumes/volume%2027/27-2-Hjelholt(web).pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)","Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Blegind","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5733d9c1-e4a9-426d-84bb-a5d5dd1a8973","name":"Jensen, Tina Blegind","orcid":"0000-0003-3095-1344","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09050167"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","pages":"3-26","paperid":"1","publisher":"The IRIS Association (Information Systems Research in Scandinavia), the Scandinavian chapter of the Association for Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84952773872"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-655003c9-6f4b-4adb-a2d8-467011b8c2f2","itu-547f4d5a-db69-4dd7-b3e6-709bca4adcf4"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Resonating Statements : Discursive Acts in IT Projects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.84-031604","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754071"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discourses at work the making and patching of organizational crevices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106145704/ssrn-2174904.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754071","ids":["itu-50e4243c-e6f0-48bd-a6e1-535569678df8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E50CA502CAF672D5223CD9997E734559"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106145704/ssrn-2174904.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Thematic Track: Language and Communication at Work: Discourse, Narrativity and Organizing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-50e4243c-e6f0-48bd-a6e1-535569678df8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discourses at Work : The Making and Patching of Organizational Crevices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754071","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Th e emergence of social network sites as a part of everyday life has given rise to a number of debates on the demo-cratic potential aff orded by these technologies. Th is paper addresses political participation facilitated through Facebook from a practice-oriented perspective and presents a case study of the political grassroots organisation, Fight For Th e Future. Initially, the paper provides a basic theoretical framework that seeks to map the relation between civic practices, materiality, and discursive features. Using this framework, the article analyses Fight For Th e Future’s use of Facebook to facilitate political participation. Th e study fi nds that user participation on the Facebook page is ‘ double conditioned’ by the material structure of the social network site on the one hand and by the discourses articulated by the organisation and users on the other. Finally, the paper discusses the fi ndings and raises a number of problems and obstacles facing participatory grassroots organisations, such as Fight For Th e Future, when using Facebook.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schou, Jannick","Farkas, Johan","Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-098.35-673006"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Participation discourse double conditioning power relations materiality Facebook case study grassroots politics"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the double conditioning of political participation grassroots politics on facebook conjunctions","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/tjcp.v2i2.22921","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.35-673006","ids":["itu-e3da9163-e5f1-4c64-91d2-fcabca365443","ku-0b91efae-0614-4d3a-8f4b-8a8e7c36253c"],"keyword":["Participation; discourse; double conditioning; power relations; materiality; Facebook; case study; grassroots politics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD79129D0DA72738B353E605374CB704"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/tjcp.v2i2.22921","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81817120/22921_52284_1_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannick","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Jannick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Johan","key":"farkaspau","last":"Farkas","locid":"18f040cd-d268-4091-88fd-eb5e46903222","name":"Farkas, Johan","orcid":"0000-0003-2272-7174","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/tjcp.v2i2.22921","issn":["22463755"],"issue":"2","journal":"Conjunctions : transdisciplinary journal of cultural participation","pages":"29-47","publisher":"Aarhus Universitet","status":"p","title":"Conjunctions : transdisciplinary journal of cultural participation","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e3da9163-e5f1-4c64-91d2-fcabca365443","ku-0b91efae-0614-4d3a-8f4b-8a8e7c36253c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Double Conditioning of Political Participation: Grassroots Politics on Facebook. Conjunctions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.35-673006","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
