sh Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-88ad9307-7baa-4641-82aa-eb36321eb7ed"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rodney Benson: Shaping Immigration News A French – American comparison. Cambridge University Press 2013","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754080","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Democratic theorists have long argued that active vigilant citizens, who watch over the state, as society‘s watchdogs, strengthen democracy. The image of the watchful eye of the people has been a central and contrasting image to the dystopian Orwellian image of Big Brother. It employs control mechanisms similar to those described by Foucault, but in the service of society. From this perspective democracy is seen as a composite of two realms – a sphere of electoral representation and a constellation of counter-democratic organizations – in constant tension with each other (Rosanvallon 2008). The watchful eyes of counter-democratic organizations are particularly made powerful by the rise of the Internet with its spontaneous adaption of watchful functions. However increased awareness and mistrust have led not to broader participation in traditional liberal institutions but to a greater social attention and demand for transparency of information. This paper takes a closer look at dynamics of counter-democratic surveillance from the perspective of a local political institution. The paper reports on a 3-year research project on counter-democratic functions of institutional oversight and organised distrust. Even though Government officials, over the three years of research, seemed to expand their overseeing legitimacy e.g. through the use of ―Big Data‖ techniques, local institutions continued to inspect, monitor, investigate and evaluate the actions of Government. Local accounts were created in the interest of the national overseers but correspondingly given as responds to fulfill legal requirements or more loosely defined public concerns. Consequently the watchful eye of a local institution form a counter-democratic sight aimed at the strategic intentions of the Government. The paper introduces the concepts of vigilance, denunciation and evaluations to explain how counter-democratic surveillance is often an overlooked feature when portraying surveillance as part of democratic promises and problems.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383477"],"event":{"end":"2014-04-26","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2014-04-24","title":"The 6th Biannual International Surveillance &amp; Society conference","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Counter democracy","Democracy","Surveillance","Transparency","Vigilance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"counter democratic surveillance the watchful eye of a local institution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ssn2014.net/blog/wp-content/uploads/booklet-20140312.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383477","ids":["itu-969322e4-0908-4acf-aeb7-7f35f1e6fc15"],"keyword":["Counter-democracy","Democracy","Surveillance","Transparency","Vigilance"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-17ACA15D26631CA794A9BCB6BA36F879"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ssn2014.net/blog/wp-content/uploads/booklet-20140312.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"10e4fc8e-556f-4104-b744-409caedc2276","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"69-70","publisher":"Universitat de Barcelona","status":"p","subtitle":"6th Biannual conference of the Surveillance Studies Network - SURVEILLANCE: AMBIGUITIES AND ASYMMETRIES","title":"ABSTRACT BOOKLET"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-969322e4-0908-4acf-aeb7-7f35f1e6fc15"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Counter-Democratic Surveillance: The Watchful Eye of a Local Institution","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383477","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Over the last three decades, EU regulation of the internal market has become highly pervasive, affecting practically all the domains of European citizens’ lives. Many studies have focused on understanding the process and causes of regulatory reform. However, these have typically been small-scale or small-n studies, with no or limited attempts to analyse the more general sources of regulatory reform. In this paper, we focus on the determinants of stability and change in EU regulation. We develop an original dataset of 169 pieces of legislation (regulations, directives and decisions) across eight different sectors, and analyse the dynamics of regulatory reform in the EU. Using time series analysis of count data, we find evidence that the number of winning coalitions in the Council and the size of EU membership have a significant impact on regulatory reform in the EU. However, the political (left-right) composition of EU’s legislative bodies has no significant impact on the process of regulatory reform.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Damsgaard, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-291677"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling the genesis and evolution","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58852229/Hjelholt_ITM_Com_12013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-291677","ids":["cbs-ab643790-cfac-4a3c-9434-4ee79e7345fd"],"keyword":["Digital payment cards","Strategic technology evolution","Technology transitions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-90218794225