819","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates how discourse can be mobilized as a strategic resource when introducing a public sector reform program in a local government setting. We explore how actual day-to-day practices, contexts, and processes relate to the shaping and localizing of broad strategic discourses. In particular, we emphasize the practices in which national strategic formulations are legitimized and accepted or abandoned by the actors involved. Building on a case study conducted over a two-year time span, we show how a local actor engages with and promotes a national reform program by evoking a discourse with strategic intentions. First we present how the national reform program is translated into a local government by the evoking of historically produced and context dependent discourses. Next we show that locally produced discourses need to be evoked and re-attached to the national reform program in order to enable new local practices. Our study shows that formal reform programs and strategies are never stable and firm objects; rather, they are constantly enacted and changed as part of discursive practices. Thus individuals enter a discursive space from where to engage strategically with the creation of new local practices.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Jensen, Tina Blegind"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-290009"],"event":{"end":"2012-07-07","place":"Helsinki, fi","start":"2012-07-05","title":"The 28th EGOS Colloquium 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Discourse","Organizational practices","Strategy"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"national reform programs in local practices using discourse as a strategic resource","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58852801/Blegind_Jensen_EGOS.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-290009","ids":["cbs-99319147-0dc9-46e2-ac67-127da3384289"],"keyword":["Discourse","Organizational practices","Public sector institutions","Strategy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E3CCD5FE6DCD9C1ED094FF7062839453"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/58852801/Blegind_Jensen_EGOS.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"fdaf290a-0e56-48a5-8afc-dc8d44fdbf3e","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Blegind","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5733d9c1-e4a9-426d-84bb-a5d5dd1a8973","name":"Jensen, Tina Blegind","orcid":"0000-0003-3095-1344","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-99319147-0dc9-46e2-ac67-127da3384289"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"National Reform Programs in Local Practices : Using Discourse as a Strategic Resource","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-290009","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Payment transactions through the use of physical coins, bank notes or credit cards have for centuries been the standard formats of exchanging money. Recently online and mobile digital payment platforms has entered the stage as contenders to this position and possibly could penetrate societies thoroughly and substitute current payment standards in the decades to come. This paper portrays how digital payment paltforms evolve in socio-technical niches and how various technological platforms aim for institutional attention in their attempt to challenge earlier platforms and standards. The paper applies a co-evolutionary multilevel perspective to model the interplay and processes between technology and society wherein digital payment platforms potentially will substitute other payment platforms just like the credit card negated the check. On this basis this paper formulate a multilevel conceptual framework and shows, through examples of new digital payment platforms, how transitions and substitutions might occur. Finally we discuss how possible venues and routes of transitions appear in the genesis and evolution of digital payment platforms.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hjelholt, Morten","Damsgaard, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-292855"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-13","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2012-06-10","title":"20th European Conference on Information Systems, ECIS 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital payment platforms","Evolution","Transitions"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genesis and evolution of digital payment platforms","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1059&context=ecis2012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-292855","identifier":[{"id":"84905748788","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-b7dcdef6-126c-4cf7-b8e2-ff0a5041f3aa"],"keyword":["Digital payment platforms","Evolution","Technology substitution","Transitions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CFFC82190AB95D81577373F7673C87B7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Intercultural Communication and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hjelholtpau","last":"Hjelholt","locid":"fdaf290a-0e56-48a5-8afc-dc8d44fdbf3e","name":"Hjelholt, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","locid":"97c6e5ec-b082-4a41-a238-69fe8cdf2a1d","name":"Damsgaard, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-7504-1937","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"prieshejepedh","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Jan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mike","key":"chiassonpedh","last":"Chiasson","name":"Chiasson, Mike","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonathan","key":"warehampedh","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Jonathan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Xavier","key":"busquetspedh","last":"Busquets","name":"Busquets, Xavier","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Josep","key":"valorpedh","last":"Valor","name":"Valor, Josep","rank":7,"role":"Editor of H